---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import site from '../site.config.ts';
import { url } from '../lib/url.ts';
---
<Page title="About" description={`About ${site.name}: a free converter for treadmill speed and running pace.`}>
  <p>{site.name} turns a treadmill speed into a running pace, and a pace into the speed to set on the belt. It works in miles and kilometers: mph, km/h, minutes per mile and minutes per kilometer.</p>
  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <p>You type a speed or a pace. The other value updates as you type. You also get the nearest speed a treadmill can really hold (most step by 0.1), finish times for a 5K, 10K, half marathon and marathon, and an estimate of the flat-ground pace that matches a treadmill incline.</p>
  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>Speed and pace are two ways to say the same thing, so the math is exact: pace in minutes equals 60 divided by speed. One mile is 1.609344 kilometers. The incline estimate uses the American College of Sports Medicine (ACSM) running equation. It is an estimate for steady running, not a measurement of your effort.</p>
  <p>The converter runs in your browser and does not send what you type. We do not ask you to create an account. Your last settings stay on your device.</p>
  <h2>A note on training</h2>
  <p>This tool helps with arithmetic. It is not medical advice. Check your treadmill's own display, because belts can read a little fast or slow. Talk to a doctor before you start a hard training plan if you have a health concern.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions or ideas? Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or visit the <a href={url('contact/')}>Contact page</a>.</p>
</Page>
